🚀 Step 2: Add Dynamic Support (IMPORTANT)
Now we modify template:

# templates/deployment.yaml
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      volumes:
        - name: config
          configMap:
            name: airflow-config

        {{- if .Values.apiServer.extraVolumes }}
        {{- toYaml .Values.apiServer.extraVolumes | nindent 8 }}
        {{- end }}
🔍 Explanation Line-by-Line (VERY SIMPLE)
✅ 1. Condition Check
{{- if .Values.apiServer.extraVolumes }}
👉 Means:

"Only run below code IF user provided extraVolumes in values.yaml"

✅ 2. Convert to YAML
toYaml .Values.apiServer.extraVolumes
👉 Converts this:

- name: airflow-dags
  hostPath:
    path: /opt/airflow/dags
👉 Into valid YAML string

✅ 3. Fix Indentation
| nindent 8
👉 Adds correct spacing so YAML is valid under volumes:

✅ 4. End Block
{{- end }}
👉 Ends the condition

📦 Step 3: VolumeMounts (ALSO REQUIRED)
You MUST also support mounts:

containers:
  - name: airflow
    image: airflow:latest

    volumeMounts:
      - name: config
        mountPath: /opt/airflow/config

      {{- if .Values.apiServer.extraVolumeMounts }}
      {{- toYaml .Values.apiServer.extraVolumeMounts | nindent 12 }}
      {{- end }}
🎯 Step 4: Final Output (What Kubernetes Sees)
After Helm runs:

volumes:
  - name: config
    configMap:
      name: airflow-config

  - name: airflow-dags
    hostPath:
      path: /opt/airflow/dags
🔁 Step 5: Why You Repeat for Scheduler / Workers
Because each component has separate template:

You must write SAME logic in:

scheduler-deployment.yaml

worker-deployment.yaml

triggerer-deployment.yaml

Example:

{{- if .Values.scheduler.extraVolumes }}
{{- toYaml .Values.scheduler.extraVolumes | nindent 8 }}
{{- end }}
🧪 Step 6: Minimal Working Example (You Can Try)
✅ values.yaml
