👉 Mounting certificates using Kubernetes Secrets in Apache Airflow Helm chart

This is how real DevOps engineers do it (not hostPath).

🧠 Why NOT hostPath (Quick Reminder)
❌ hostPath problems:

Node dependent

Not portable

Not secure

✅ Best practice:
👉 Use Kubernetes Secret

🎯 Goal
You want:

Certificates → stored securely → mounted inside Airflow pods
🧱 Step 1: Create Secret (Certificate Storage)
Assume you have:

server.crt
server.key
Create secret:

kubectl create secret generic airflow-certs \
  --from-file=server.crt \
  --from-file=server.key
👉 Kubernetes stores it like:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: airflow-certs
🏗️ Step 2: Use Helm values.yaml (NO template change)
Now create your custom values file:

# values-secret.yaml

apiServer:
  extraVolumes:
    - name: airflow-certs
      secret:
        secretName: airflow-certs

  extraVolumeMounts:
    - name: airflow-certs
      mountPath: /opt/airflow/certs
      readOnly: true

scheduler:
  extraVolumes:
    - name: airflow-certs
      secret:
        secretName: airflow-certs

  extraVolumeMounts:
    - name: airflow-certs
      mountPath: /opt/airflow/certs
      readOnly: true

workers:
  extraVolumes:
    - name: airflow-certs
      secret:
        secretName: airflow-certs

  extraVolumeMounts:
    - name: airflow-certs
      mountPath: /opt/airflow/certs
      readOnly: true
🚀 Step 3: Deploy
helm upgrade airflow apache-airflow/airflow -f values-secret.yaml
🔍 Step 4: What Helm Does Internally
Template (already in chart):

volumes:
  {{- if .Values.scheduler.extraVolumes }}
  {{- toYaml .Values.scheduler.extraVolumes | nindent 8 }}
  {{- end }}
👉 Your values get injected:

- name: airflow-certs
  secret:
    secretName: airflow-certs
📦 Final Kubernetes YAML (IMPORTANT)
volumes:
  - name: airflow-certs
    secret:
      secretName: airflow-certs
And:

volumeMounts:
  - name: airflow-certs
    mountPath: /opt/airflow/certs
    readOnly: true
⚙️ Step 5: What Kubernetes Does
👉 Kubernetes automatically:

Reads Secret airflow-certs

Converts each key into file

Mounts inside container

📁 Inside Container You’ll See:
/opt/airflow/certs/
  server.crt
  server.key
🔁 Full Flow (VERY IMPORTANT)
kubectl create secret
        ↓
values.yaml (extraVolumes)
        ↓
Helm template injects
        ↓
Kubernetes mounts secret
        ↓
Airflow container reads certs
🧪 Step 6: Verify
kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -- ls /opt/airflow/certs
✔️ Output:

server.crt
server.key
🔥 Real DevOps Insight
👉 You didn’t modify ANY template
👉 Only used:

extraVolumes
extraVolumeMounts
This is called:

Helm Chart Extensibility
⚠️ Common Mistakes
❌ Secret not created
→ Pod will fail

❌ Wrong secret name
secretName: wrong-name ❌
❌ Missing mountPath
→ Volume exists but not usable

🧠 Final Mental Model
Secret = secure storage
extraVolumes = attach secret
extraVolumeMounts = use inside container
Helm = inject config
Kubernetes = mount as files
